/A 2174 0 R
/Alt (Panel a shows a diagram explaining Raman and Rayleigh scattering, with incident light interacting with a molecule, resulting in different energy scatterings corresponding to Rayleigh, Stokes, and anti-Stokes Raman events shown as arrows in an energy level diagram. Panel b provides schematic representations of three Raman spectroscopy setups: a laboratory system with labeled optical paths and components, a simplified optical bench configuration, and a handheld probe setup. Panel c displays false-color images mapping spectral features at specific Raman shifts and autofluorescence in tissue samples, with each image labeled by its spectral wavenumber or emission property. Panel d features photographs of liver tissue with marked regions, corresponding false-color segmented images distinguishing carcinoma and parenchyma, and graphs comparing Raman spectral shifts from different tissue regions, with annotations and color-coded traces.)
