/A 2234 0 R
/Alt (Panel a contains four overlaid Raman spectra for metastasis, normal lymph node tissue, adipose tissue, capsule, and red blood cells, each with distinct spectral features. Panel b shows a histology slide of tissue \(i\), associated Raman spectra \(ii, v\), colored intensity heat maps \(iii, vi\), and a grayscale close-up \(iv\). Panel c displays Raman spectral analysis, including two line graphs comparing benign, secondary, and primary tumors \(i, ii\), and a scatter plot showing classification by spectral features \(iii\). Panel d presents two stimulated Raman scattering \(SRS\) images of primary papillary thyroid carcinoma and lymphatic metastasis, each labeled and with scale bars, next to two Raman spectra comparing lymphatic metastasis and glyceryl trioleate.)
/K [0 2235 0 R]
/P 109 0 R
/Pg 55 0 R
/S /Figure
