/A 2331 0 R
/Alt (Scientific infographic illustrating surface-enhanced Raman scattering \(SERS\) mechanisms and nanoparticle configurations. Panel a shows SERS process with incident light causing Stokes and anti-Stokes scattering from molecules on a gold surface. Panel b depicts electric field enhancement near metal nanoparticles. Panel c outlines five methods for SERS signal enhancement including resonance and substrate effects. Panel d details stages of SERS probe synthesis: i, metal nanoparticle types; ii, attachment of Raman reporters; iii, application of protective coatings such as silica, polymers, phospholipids, membranes, and proteins; iv, functionalization with targeting ligands like drugs, antibodies, aptamers, nucleic acids, and peptides.)
